# Credential names only. Never a real value -- see integrations/CREDENTIALS.md.
#
# scripts/onboard.sh copies this to .env.local (already gitignored) and
# prints each name below so a new person knows what to go get. Setting a
# real value happens outside this repo: a password manager, or a Windows
# user environment variable, per CREDENTIALS.md's "Where Values Actually
# Live" section.
#
# Nothing is listed below yet because no integration in this workspace has
# a credential wired up: Google Workspace is an account connector with no
# key to hold (see integrations/google-workspace.md), and
# accounting/banking is not yet connected (see
# departments/finance/integrations/accounting-banking.md). When an
# integration that needs a credential is installed, add its variable name
# here -- name only, per integrations/INSTALLING.md's `${VAR_NAME}` rule
# for .mcp.json entries. Example shape once one exists:
#
# EXAMPLE_API_KEY=
#
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY is not listed here on purpose, even though it is a
# real, named credential (see integrations/anthropic-api.md). Its only
# consumer is CI running scripts/run-department.sh, and it lives as a
# GitHub Actions repository secret, never as a value on this machine or in
# .env.local. See _company/autonomy.md.
